# ${{ values.serviceName }}

This repository holds the Terraform configuration of the Azure API Management
instance `${{ values.serviceName }}`. Nothing exists in Azure until the Deploy
workflow has credentials; see [Deployment](deployment.md).

## Endpoints after deployment

| Endpoint | URL |
| --- | --- |
| Gateway | `https://${{ values.serviceName }}.azure-api.net` |
{%- if portal %}
| Developer portal | `https://${{ values.serviceName }}.developer.azure-api.net` |
{%- endif %}

## Settings chosen at creation

The current settings are in `infra/terraform.tfvars` and
`infra/apis.auto.tfvars.json`; this table is not updated when they change.

| Setting | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Pricing tier | ${{ sku }} |
| Region | `${{ values.location or "eastus" }}` |
| Developer portal | ${{ "Open" if portal else "Closed" }} |
| Portal requires sign-in | ${{ "Yes" if portalAuth else "No" }} |
| Microsoft Entra ID sign-in on the portal | ${{ "Yes" if entra else "No" }} |
| JWT validation on every API | ${{ "Yes" if jwt else "No" }} |
| Rate limit per subscription | ${{ (values.callsPerMinute or 1000) ~ " calls per minute" if rateLimit else "None" }} |
| CORS | ${{ "Yes" if cors else "No" }} |
| Response caching | ${{ "Yes" if caching else "No" }} |
| Application Insights | ${{ "Yes" if appInsights else "No" }} |
| Log Analytics | ${{ (values.logRetention or 90) ~ " days retention" if logAnalytics else "No" }} |
| APIs | ${{ apis | length }} |
{% if sku == "Developer" %}
!!! warning "Developer tier"
    The Developer tier has no SLA and a single unit. Microsoft does not support
    it for production traffic.
{% endif %}
{%- if sku == "Basic" and entra and portal %}
!!! warning "No Microsoft Entra ID sign-in in the Basic tier"
    The Basic tier does not offer Microsoft Entra ID as an identity provider of
    the developer portal, so the identity provider and its app registration are
    not created. Developers sign in with a user name and password. Change `sku`
    to `Developer`, `Standard` or `Premium` to get Microsoft Entra ID sign-in.
{% endif %}
{%- if entra and not portal %}
!!! note "Microsoft Entra ID sign-in needs the portal"
    Microsoft Entra ID sign-in applies to the developer portal, which is closed
    here. Set `enable_portal = true` to have the identity provider created.
{% endif %}
{%- if appInsights and not logAnalytics %}
!!! note "Log Analytics workspace"
    Application Insights stores its data in a Log Analytics workspace, so a
    workspace is created although Log Analytics is switched off. Gateway logs
    and metrics are not sent to it.
{% endif %}
## What is deployed

| Resource | Created when |
| --- | --- |
| Resource group `rg-<service_name>-<environment>-<location>` | Always |
| API Management instance with a system-assigned identity | Always |
| Global policy (CORS, JWT validation, caching) | Always; contains only the enabled policies |
| Product `<service_name>` that requires a subscription | Always |
| One API per entry of `apis`, attached to the product | Per entry |
| Product policy with the rate limit | `enable_rate_limiting` |
| App registration, client secret and Microsoft Entra ID identity provider | `enable_portal` and `enable_azure_ad`, except in the Basic tier |
| Log Analytics workspace | `enable_log_analytics` or `enable_application_insights` |
| Diagnostic setting for gateway logs and metrics | `enable_log_analytics` |
| Application Insights, logger and diagnostic | `enable_application_insights` |

[Configuration](configuration.md) describes each setting.

## Pipelines

| Workflow | Runs | Needs credentials |
| --- | --- | --- |
| CI | Formatting, validation, a test against mocked providers, tflint, Trivy and the documentation build | No |
| Deploy | Terraform plan on every push and pull request, apply on `main` | Yes; plan and apply are skipped until they are configured |
